## SQ-FO-12 | flavor crafts: type, ids, tags; no seasoning leftovers
@group A
@commands `cdevtest bytype creativedelight:flavor`; `cdevtest recipes shapeless/season/`; tag probe `creativedelight:flavorable/onion`; grep latest.log for `[flavor] defined` and `[flavor] pair`
@pass flavor crafts exist with ids `creativedelight:shapeless/flavor/...` (cheese, onion, garlic, ghost_pepper, void_pepper, onion_garlic, the six BBQ ones and the four new sauces); no `shapeless/season/` recipe; `creativedelight:flavorable/onion` holds popcorn; latest.log lists 17 `[flavor] defined` and 3 `[flavor] pair` lines, no `[flavor] bad definition`
@fails CD `food/FlavorRecipe` (serializer `flavor`), Common NCH `flavor()`, data `flavor.js`, `flavor_tags.js`; startup `flavors.js`
@absent creativedelight:flavor (a recipe type, not an item)
> cdevtest bytype creativedelight:flavor
> cdevtest recipes shapeless/season/
> cdevtest tag item creativedelight:flavorable/onion
waitlog verb=tag kind=item tag=creativedelight:flavorable/onion n= 30
expect verb=bytype .*n=[1-9]
reject verb=recipes text=shapeless/season/ n=[1-9]
expect verb=tag kind=item tag=creativedelight:flavorable/onion n=\d+ ids=.*corn_delight:popcorn
shell test "$(grep -c "\[flavor\] defined" logs/latest.log)" -ge 17
shell test "$(grep -c "\[flavor\] pair" logs/latest.log)" -ge 3
shell ! grep -q "\[flavor\] bad definition" logs/latest.log
reject verb=\S+ .*done=0

## SQ-FO-13 | flavor values: +2 saturation each, pairs +1, Grilled slots
@group A
@commands as a bot: craft popcorn + onion + garlic (or give `corn_delight:popcorn{Flavors:["creativedelight:garlic","creativedelight:onion"]}`), set food 10 / saturation 0, eat; then a plain flavored popcorn; give a grilled skewer with Grilled and 4 flavors and check it holds them
@pass onion + garlic popcorn: saturation rises by popcorn's own + 5 (2 + 2 + 1 pair), Speed 10 s; one flavor: +2; nutrition only the popcorn's; a food with Grilled takes up to 4 flavors (maxFlavors 2 + grilledFlavorSlots 2), without Grilled 2
@fails `Flavors.applyEaten` / `pairSaturation` / `cap`; CDConfig `[food] maxFlavors`, `grilledFlavorSlots`
@draft needs a bot eat with set food and saturation reads (/pbot eat, data get entity); the first runner writes the steps

